WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.860
The pipeline begins with sparse input face images under varied illumination, utilizing four core processing operations outlined in the legend.

2
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:13.490
A three-dimensional morphable model is first fitted to establish an initial geometric proxy model.

3
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.760
This proxy geometry is then analyzed to extract surface orientations and anatomical regions.

4
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.020
A dense normal map captures the underlying surface directions across the facial structure.

5
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:30.030
Semantic segmentation categorizes different facial zones, distinguishing bare skin from regions like hair and eyes.

6
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:35.290
Dedicated shadow processing identifies and handles cast shadows to ensure accurate lighting estimation.

7
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:41.300
Using light calibration and photometric stereo, the geometry is reconstructed into a refined 3D model.

8
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.190
In the final stage, region-tailored denoising is applied across the reconstructed outputs.

9
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:51.830
This yields a high-fidelity denoised 3D facial mesh alongside a clean surface albedo map.

